Patch 08 -- spend the hot-page budget only on addresses in the hot page.

`SetHotPage()` marks one page as recently self-modifying and gives it a budget of
HOTPAGE_MARK checks; `isInHotPage()` is asked about an address on the dynarec's
protection path. The original decremented the budget on EVERY call, including
calls about addresses in some other page entirely, so unrelated traffic spent the
budget of the page that actually needed it and the hot page fell back to full
protection early.

The change is order-of-operations only: test membership first, and charge the
budget only for a hit. It cannot make isInHotPage() return true where it
returned false; it can only keep it true for longer on the page it is about.

NOT MEASURED. There is no A/B for this patch: it went into
`box86-island32-hotpage` and then into the production `box86-island32-prod`
without a frame-rate arm on either. Treat it as an unmeasured change that is
currently deployed, not as a win. `box86-island31` is the last binary without it.

Verifiable without a disassembler: this hunk alone is what separates
`box86-island32-hotpage` from `box86-island31`, and patch 09 is what separates
`box86-island32-prod` from `box86-island32-hotpage` -- .tbss is 0x294 bytes in
both of the first two and 0x2a4 in prod.

--- a/src/custommem.c
+++ b/src/custommem.c
@@ -893,8 +893,10 @@
 {
     if(!hotpage_cnt)
         return 0;
+    if(addr < hotpage || addr >= hotpage + box86_pagesize)
+        return 0;
     --hotpage_cnt;
-    return (addr>=hotpage) && (addr<hotpage+box86_pagesize);
+    return 1;
 }
 int checkInHotPage(uintptr_t addr)
 {
